WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.620
Gravitational waves from white dwarf pairs may reveal hidden exoplanets through frequency sidebands that Lisa can detect. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 251, an independent check of the M87 ring, Uranus and Neptune's tangled magnetism, and cosmic spotlight follow. Casey McGrath, a postdoctoral researcher at the University of Maryland, Baltimore County, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, Goddard Space Flight Center,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.060
StarLust.org reports published in the Astrophysical Journal on November 10th, 2026.

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:42.625
One paper charts the conditions that favor a detection, and the other works out how the

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:45.525
James Webb Space Telescope can confirm a candidate.

00:00:46.065 --> 00:00:50.685
When two white dwarfs circle each other in under an hour, they pour out a gravitational

00:00:50.685 --> 00:00:52.805
wave tone that stays nearly constant.

00:00:53.724 --> 00:00:58.444
The Milky Way holds roughly 10 million of these pairs, and Lisa should separate about

00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:00.964
about 10,000 of them as individual sources.

00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:04.244
Marianne Limbach, an assistant research scientist

00:01:04.244 --> 00:01:06.884
at the University of Michigan, and a co-author

00:01:06.884 --> 00:01:09.144
on the second paper, stressed that pairing

00:01:09.144 --> 00:01:11.564
the two observatories is how genuine planets

00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:13.464
get separated from false positives.

00:01:14.529 --> 00:01:17.369
Webb's infrared reach can pick up a planet of five

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:20.189
Jupiter masses at least 500 light years away.

00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:24.809
A triangle of spacecraft each side 2.5 million kilometers

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:28.169
will drift behind Earth, and every tiny change

00:01:28.169 --> 00:01:32.529
in those distances will be tracked to a precision finer than the width of a helium atom.

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:37.709
When a planet circles the pair, its gravity tugs the white dwarfs into a slight wobble,

00:01:38.169 --> 00:01:42.209
and that motion writes extra frequencies just above and below the main tone.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:47.509
The same way a radio carrier wave carries audio off to either side of the center frequency.

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:53.189
Lisa is also expected to pick out roughly 100 mixed binaries that pair a white dwarf

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:55.729
with a black hole or a neutron star.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:02:01.369
Under favorable conditions, the sideband pattern can betray a companion as small as sub-Jupiter

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:06.329
mass, and a matching infrared detection would show the gravitational wave signature belongs

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:11.109
to a planet, rather than an instrumental artifact or an unseen third star.

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:16.969
The method mirrors the radial velocity trick already used with starlight, except the wobble

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:21.789
is read in ripples of spacetime instead of in spectral lines, and those ripples travel

00:02:21.789 --> 00:02:23.829
through dust and gas without being blocked.

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:29.909
The expected signal strength for a Jupiter mass companion can already be calculated, yet nobody

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:34.849
knows how often such companions actually sit around double white dwarfs, or what that

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:39.489
rate would say about worlds surviving the violent evolution that strips stars down to white

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:40.709
dwarfs in the first place.

00:02:41.638 --> 00:02:47.978
A team of four from CSIRO, Fizz.org reports, developed a new imaging technique that validated

00:02:47.978 --> 00:02:54.498
the 2019 Event Horizon Telescope image of the Black Hole at the center of Galaxy M87.

00:02:55.038 --> 00:02:58.778
That reconstruction captured the first direct view of a Black Hole shadow.

00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:04.658
The 2019 picture became one of the most recognized scientific images of the modern era,

00:03:05.078 --> 00:03:09.518
and the CSIRO method offers an independent check on the original reconstruction

00:03:09.518 --> 00:03:14.778
produced by hundreds of scientists. The work adds confidence that the observed ring structure

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:19.078
accurately reflects the black hole environment rather than processing artifacts.

00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:28.045
Uranus and Neptune, Universe Today Reports, have interiors unlike the other planets and therefore possess messy, tilted magnetic fields.

00:03:28.705 --> 00:03:34.285
Voyager 2 remains the only spacecraft to have flown by them and revealed how irregular those fields are.

00:03:34.885 --> 00:03:43.185
New models suggest the fields change on very short time scales and could already differ from their state during the Voyager 2 encounters in the late 1980s.

00:03:43.185 --> 00:03:49.105
The research uses updated interior models to explore why the ice giants generate such complex

00:03:49.105 --> 00:03:53.705
magnetic environments compared with the more orderly fields of earth and the gas giants.

00:03:54.681 --> 00:04:00.381
Atmospheric Argon 40 on Uranus and Neptune, Fizz.org reports, can estimate the amount of

00:04:00.381 --> 00:04:04.761
rock beneath their surfaces and supply clues about where and how the planets formed.

00:04:05.361 --> 00:04:09.881
A Southwest Research Institute team led the study published in the Planetary Science

00:04:09.881 --> 00:04:10.241
Journal.

00:04:10.241 --> 00:04:15.981
The argon isotope ratio serves as a tracer for the bulk composition of the planet's interiors.

00:04:16.361 --> 00:04:22.541
The team aims to distinguish between formation scenarios that place the ice giants closer to the sun before migration,

00:04:23.101 --> 00:04:24.901
and formation in place farther out.

00:04:25.848 --> 00:04:29.868
The supermassive black hole in Centaurus A, 12 million light years away,

00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:33.368
hurls two enormous plasma jets at nearly the speed of light.

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:38.748
Plasma simulations now explain why those jets appear brighter at their edges than at their centers,

00:04:38.748 --> 00:04:43.108
measures, a pattern that had puzzled observers since the jets were first imaged in detail.

00:04:43.768 --> 00:04:48.268
The work comes from the chair of astronomy at the University of Würzberg, and appears

00:04:48.268 --> 00:04:49.868
in astronomy and astrophysics.

00:04:50.468 --> 00:04:54.548
The new models reproduce the observed brightness pattern through the interaction of magnetic

00:04:54.548 --> 00:04:57.528
fields and particle acceleration within the jet structure.

00:04:58.415 --> 00:05:04.815
China launched a CZ2D rocket, Space News reports, on November 11th carrying the Tan Lujet

00:05:04.815 --> 00:05:05.775
Science Satellite.

00:05:05.775 --> 00:05:09.695
The satellite carries three sub-satellites that will be deployed later.

00:05:10.275 --> 00:05:15.095
The mission tests key instruments for upcoming flagship space science missions, including

00:05:15.095 --> 00:05:16.775
a lunar orbiting radio array.

00:05:17.335 --> 00:05:22.775
The flight forms part of a technology demonstration effort ahead of larger science projects, and

00:05:22.775 --> 00:05:28.315
the four satellite payload focuses on instruments destined for future Chinese space science flagships.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:35.028
NASA officials are as technical reports, outlined multiple lunar contract awards and opportunities

00:05:35.028 --> 00:05:39.148
in a single weekend, including landers, nuclear-powered rovers,

00:05:39.668 --> 00:05:43.088
scouting drones, power systems, and communication satellites.

00:05:43.628 --> 00:05:48.088
The agency is using broad agency announcements and a two-step proposal process

00:05:48.088 --> 00:05:52.608
to reach companies of all sizes, including those that have not yet flown hardware.

00:05:53.168 --> 00:05:57.908
Mike Gold, President of Redwire Space and former NASA Associate Administrator,

00:05:58.408 --> 00:06:01.168
described the pace of solicitations as unprecedented.

00:06:01.168 --> 00:06:06.968
NASA is deliberately diversifying its supplier base rather than relying on a small number

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:11.688
of traditional primes, and the approach includes orbital transfer vehicles from impulse

00:06:11.688 --> 00:06:18.088
space and large rockets from relativity space. K2 space is developing large satellites,

00:06:18.468 --> 00:06:23.448
NBC News reports, intended for future Mars missions and other deep space applications.

00:06:24.088 --> 00:06:29.068
The company focuses on platforms that could support cargo delivery, communications, or

00:06:29.068 --> 00:06:34.108
scientific instruments on long-duration journeys. The work aligns with broader industry

00:06:34.108 --> 00:06:37.508
efforts to scale up spacecraft for interplanetary logistics.

00:06:38.554 --> 00:06:43.714
A Senate committee, Space News Reports, is preparing to advance nominations for NASA's

00:06:43.714 --> 00:06:48.954
Chief Financial Officer and Inspector General. The nominations address key leadership roles

00:06:48.954 --> 00:06:52.894
responsible for budget oversight and internal accountability at the agency.

00:06:53.514 --> 00:06:58.294
Confirmation would fill positions that guide financial management during ongoing lunar and

00:06:58.294 --> 00:07:04.802
Mars program development. Indian student Pritha Jaipal, Frontline magazine reports, is participating

00:07:04.802 --> 00:07:10.682
in the Eskipio 6 analog mission in the Swiss Alps that simulates lunar surface operations.

00:07:11.242 --> 00:07:16.302
The mission provides hands-on experience with procedures and equipment that future lunar crews may

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:21.762
use. Jaipal's involvement highlights growing international student participation in analog

00:07:21.762 --> 00:07:28.689
research programs. A conjunction captured in Poland, NASA reports, shows the crescent moon above the

00:07:28.689 --> 00:07:32.969
Tattra Mountains, Bright Venus nearby, and Spika to the left of Venus.

00:07:33.549 --> 00:07:37.349
Spika is a triple star system roughly 250 light years away.

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:41.349
Earlier this year, astronomers confirmed Spika's third companion,

00:07:41.909 --> 00:07:45.049
making it a hierarchical triple rather than a simple binary.

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:48.069
Planets appear to wander among the fixed stars,

00:07:48.289 --> 00:07:51.229
and so create conjunctions governed by celestial mechanics,

00:07:51.769 --> 00:07:54.549
and the photograph was taken by Wudzi Mirr's boobak.

00:07:54.549 --> 00:08:00.512
NASA is advancing a new Perseverance Sample Retrieval Architecture for Mars Sample Return.

00:08:01.172 --> 00:08:04.992
Global Times reports, amid discussions of international competition.

00:08:05.552 --> 00:08:10.572
The refresh plan seeks to maintain momentum on returning cash samples from the Martian surface.

00:08:11.372 --> 00:08:15.312
Experts have cautioned that framing the effort primarily as a race with China,

00:08:15.892 --> 00:08:18.412
risks undermining broader scientific cooperation.

00:08:18.412 --> 00:08:24.753
The August 12th, 2026 total solar eclipse set over the late Bronze Age settlement of

00:08:24.753 --> 00:08:27.013
Talati to Dalt on Menorca, Spain.

00:08:27.553 --> 00:08:33.393
With totality lasting roughly 73 seconds, the site's first total eclipse since 1539.

00:08:34.193 --> 00:08:39.113
Photographer Josh Dury created a composite that captures the Sun's partial phases descending

00:08:39.113 --> 00:08:43.313
toward the horizon, and the brief moment of darkness over the ancient stones.

00:08:43.313 --> 00:08:49.553
The image places the eclipse in a deep historical context, connecting a modern astronomical event

00:08:49.553 --> 00:08:53.793
with a location that last experienced totality more than four centuries earlier.

00:08:54.669 --> 00:08:59.289
From Jordan Lake in North Carolina, an image of the Pleiades cluster reveals reflection

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:03.929
nebulosity and surrounding dust after one hour and forty minutes of integration.

00:09:04.609 --> 00:09:09.229
The Senate Committee is preparing to advance NASA's Chief Financial Officer and Inspector

00:09:09.229 --> 00:09:14.369
general nominations, and confirmation would show who holds budget oversight and internal

00:09:14.369 --> 00:09:17.209
accountability as lunar and Mars programs grow.

